cation describes a single heater output through J6 and does not mention J5. A terminal wired from a GPIO control net to ground is not described as part of the design.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\"source\": \"spec\", \"quote\": \"Drives a single **heater output** net through a smart high-side switch (`U6`, TPS1H200AQDGNRQ1)\"},\n        {\"source\": \"schematic\", \"quote\": \"Page 2 (mcu.kicad_sch): 'HEATER' wired to J5 pin 2; J5 pin 1 wired to GND\"}\n      ],\n      \"impact\": \"If J5 is populated with a load or a plug-in, it places a load or short on the GPIO1 logic output and can bypass the intended heater path.\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.15\n    }\n  ],\n  \"summary\": \"The netlist matches the specification for most parts, but the feedback pin of the buck regulator U8 appears on a wire that reaches a GND node, which would short the 3.3 V output's feedback to ground. This is a low-to-moderate confidence reading of a dense drawing. The unexplained terminal J5 on the heater logic net is a weaker secondary concern.\"\n}",
